WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.240
The bristle showed what an inherited protein does.

2
00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:08.760
But how does a cell put it on one side?

3
00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:12.970
The fly neuroblast is where that machinery was worked out.

4
00:00:13.883 --> 00:00:15.643
A clue came in 1995.

5
00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:20.683
Prospero is a transcription factor, a protein that works in the nucleus.

6
00:00:21.717 --> 00:00:26.617
Yet Jürgen Knoblich and the Jans found it at the membrane in dividing cells, in the

7
00:00:26.617 --> 00:00:27.737
same crescent as Numb.

8
00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:33.030
Its position followed one centrosome, but it did not need microtubules.

9
00:00:33.710 --> 00:00:36.130
So it was not carried into place along the spindle.

10
00:00:37.133 --> 00:00:41.633
That pointed to a separate system in the cortex that marks one side of the cell.

11
00:00:42.413 --> 00:00:43.573
It works in four steps.

12
00:00:44.617 --> 00:00:47.157
Step one. Mark the top.

13
00:00:48.150 --> 00:00:51.590
Bazooka, the fly's Par3, gathers at the top cortex.

14
00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:53.990
Par6 joins it.

15
00:00:54.883 --> 00:00:56.763
So does a kinase called aPKC.

16
00:00:57.803 --> 00:00:59.143
Together they define the top side.

17
00:01:02.183 --> 00:01:04.843
Step two. Aim the spindle.

18
00:01:05.867 --> 00:01:08.087
Inscuteable joins the top complex.

19
00:01:09.007 --> 00:01:11.107
Inscuteable recruits a protein called Pins.

20
00:01:12.217 --> 00:01:17.157
Pins works with a G protein subunit, Gαi, and a protein called Mud.

21
00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:20.720
Together they anchor the motor dynein at the top.

22
00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:24.360
Dynein pulls on microtubules from one spindle pole.

23
00:01:25.383 --> 00:01:27.643
So the spindle lines up from top to bottom.

24
00:01:28.523 --> 00:01:30.463
The furrow will cut between top and bottom.

25
00:01:31.483 --> 00:01:36.143
Inscuteable is needed both to aim the spindle and to place Numb and Prospero

26
00:01:36.143 --> 00:01:37.143
correctly.

27
00:01:39.617 --> 00:01:42.657
Step three. Keep the cargo off the top.

28
00:01:43.650 --> 00:01:47.670
At the top, aPKC phosphorylates Lgl, Numb and Miranda.

29
00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:51.660
Phosphorylated proteins let go of the cortex.

30
00:01:52.180 --> 00:01:54.440
And a P K C works only at the top.

31
00:01:55.433 --> 00:01:58.833
So Numb and Miranda stay bound only at the bottom cortex.

32
00:01:59.893 --> 00:02:01.873
L G L is a helper here, not cargo.

33
00:02:02.917 --> 00:02:05.497
Step four. Carry the cargo.

34
00:02:06.550 --> 00:02:11.110
The adaptor Miranda carries Prospero, and the translational repressor Brat.

35
00:02:12.033 --> 00:02:14.673
Numb uses its own adaptor, Partner of Numb.

36
00:02:15.617 --> 00:02:20.937
The cell divides. The small daughter, the ganglion mother cell, inherits the cargo.

37
00:02:22.017 --> 00:02:26.877
Prospero enters its nucleus and shuts down genes for self-renewal and division.

38
00:02:27.917 --> 00:02:29.237
Now remove Miranda.

39
00:02:30.177 --> 00:02:31.617
Where do Prospero and Brat go?

40
00:02:32.417 --> 00:02:33.877
What happens over many divisions?

41
00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:42.440
They lose their crescent at the bottom cortex.

42
00:02:43.340 --> 00:02:45.880
Where they end up depends on the stage and the lineage.

43
00:02:46.950 --> 00:02:51.010
Larval miranda mutant tissue overgrows when transplanted.

44
00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:55.370
Faulty sorting can let small daughters keep dividing like neuroblasts.

45
00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:02.160
The sensory organ precursor divides within its epithelium.

46
00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:04.640
The neuroblast divides across it.

47
00:03:05.533 --> 00:03:08.553
But both mark one side and aim the spindle at it.

48
00:03:09.367 --> 00:03:13.707
Mark the top, aim the spindle, keep the cargo off the top, and load the small

49
00:03:13.707 --> 00:03:14.007
daughter.
